Goal: run a resilient ADB pull loop with logging and retry behavior.
```powershell
$Remote = "/sdcard/Download/report.txt"
$LocalDir = "C:\PhonePulls\batch_00"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $LocalDir | Out-Null
while ($true) {
  try {
    adb get-state | Out-Null
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "ADB device not ready" }
    adb pull $Remote $LocalDir
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "adb pull failed with exit code $LASTEXITCODE" }
    Write-Host "Pulled $Remote at $(Get-Date -Format s)"
  } catch { Write-Warning $_.Exception.Message }
  Start-Sleep -Seconds 5
}
```
Why: each command is checked, so cable drops, authorization loss, and missing files are reported instead of hidden.

Goal: collect mirroring failure details without losing the original error.
```powershell
try {
  adb get-state | Out-Null
  if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "ADB is not ready" }
  scrcpy --max-fps 30 --video-bit-rate 4M 2>&1 | Tee-Object C:\PhoneDiagnostics\scrcpy.log
} catch { Write-Error $_.Exception.Message }
```
Why: logging stderr keeps codec, firewall, and authorization errors available after the window closes.

